{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f002","f019"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s12; BRANCH=peer-trusted-transport; Search only snapshots/s12. Cross-subsystem trust-boundary analogue completing this snapshot's matrix row: find kernel-side clients or servers of remote or virtual device transports — network-exported buses, virtual HCDs, guest-host channels (drivers/hv), remote-storage/remote-fs reply handlers (9p trans_fd/virtio/rdma/xen, nbd, ceph/cifs), greybus/serdev links (gb-beagleplay, es2), rpmsg/qcom_glink, virtio/vhost ring protocols, remote admin-queue or DMA reply handlers — where allocation or iteration is driven by peer-supplied response counts/lengths, and check whether those peer fields are cross-checked against locally-known limits before use. Prior audits in sibling snapshots only enumerated 9p, nbd, virtio/vhost, and HID transports without deep-reading them: give those a real read here, including completion-time peer metadata such as urb->actual_length handed to memcpy or iteration bounds (the greybus es2.c bulk-in greybus_data_rcvd call was left unresolved by an earlier audit). Known peer-trust chains worth re-checking in this tree's state: greybus gb-beagleplay hdlc_rx_greybus_frame passing the peer le16 hdr.size while ignoring the locally known frame length; hv_balloon balloon_down consuming the host-supplied range_count with only a recvlen>0 gate; qcom_glink chunk_size/left_size validated only against SMEM head/tail written by the same peer. Identify by mechanism (peer-controlled size crossing a trust boundary into kernel allocation or loop), including callers/callees and alternative protocol framings, not by subsystem name. Record the peer-field source, the missing local limit check, and the consuming allocation/loop; a negative result must list the peer-driven handlers examined. The seed usbip path is demonstration-only and must never be reported; if unpatched usbip is present, record it as excluded-by-rule and keep searching. Save a structured artifact (execution_status, candidates or evidence-backed negative) for snapshots/s12 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f020"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s13; BRANCH=alloc-multiply-overflow; Search only snapshots/s13. Direct structural/API analogue of the seed's sizing chain: hunt a 32-bit multiply (count*element-size, count+offset, or count<<shift) computed with plain int/unsigned arithmetic from an untrusted count and passed to kmalloc/kzalloc/vmalloc/kmemdup/devm_kzalloc instead of kcalloc/array_size/struct_size, followed by an element-indexed copy/recv/memcpy loop that still trusts the original count, so the truncated product under-allocates and the loop writes past the heap buffer. Sweep driver, fs, net, block, sound, and crypto parsers within this one snapshot; prioritize counts that cross a trust boundary (wire parse, ioctl copy_from_user, device/DMA metadata, on-disk structures) over locally computed counts. Known strong shapes from sibling audits to verify in this tree's state: drivers/virt/fsl_hypervisor.c ioctl_memcpy (unsigned int num_pages = (param.count + lb_offset + PAGE_SIZE - 1) >> PAGE_SHIFT truncating the u64 ioctl count, then kmalloc(num_pages * sizeof(struct fh_sg_list) + ...) feeding a for (i = 1; i < num_pages; i++) fill loop) and block/partitions/ldm.c ldm_frag_add (kmalloc(sizeof(*f) + size*num) from the on-disk vblk_size with a rec*size memcpy; check whether the perbuf = 512/size caller bound still constrains size in this tree). For each candidate record file:line of the unchecked arithmetic, the allocator call, the consuming loop, and where the count enters from outside the kernel; a negative result must cite the allocator-adjacent arithmetic sites examined. The seed usbip_recv_iso chain itself is demonstration-only and must never be reported; if unpatched usbip code is present (int size = np * sizeof(*iso) in usbip_common.c feeding kzalloc and the iso recv loop), record it as excluded-by-rule and keep searching. Save a structured artifact (execution_status, candidates or evidence-backed negative) for snapshots/s13 only."}
